This fixture exercises phpc's MySQLi statement cursor-fetch handle validation
through a WordPress-shaped `wpdb` method. System PHP would require a real
mysqli statement object, bound result buffers, cursor advancement, and host
database rows; phpc only records the reached non-statement-object diagnostic
here. Supported placeholder statement result fetching is covered in later
fixtures and does not implement true by-reference aliasing, unbuffered
statement fetching, bound-parameter execution, real mysqlnd cursor behavior,
or host database rows.
